  "rationale": "structural: The text has three layout obligations and one delegated obligation. The roots cover each of them.\n\n- **Markdown in `md/`.** The clause is \"keep its mdBook Markdown in `md/`\". `book.toml#table[book]/pair[src]` sets `src = \"md\"`. A book with a different `src` would break this clause even if it rendered the same, so the setting is structural.\n- **`habeas` source in `src/`.** `Cargo.toml#table[lib]/pair[path]` (`src/lib.rs`) and `Cargo.toml#table[bin]/pair[path]` (`src/main.rs`) put the library and binary roots under `src/`. Pointing either path elsewhere would violate the clause.\n- **`trust-but-verify` source in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/`.** `crates/trust-but-verify/Cargo.toml#table[package]/pair[name]` is a marked root. It names the crate whose manifest sits in `crates/trust-but-verify/`. That manifest has no `[lib]` or `[[bin]]` path override, so Cargo's default `src/` applies. The source listing shows its files under `crates/trust-but-verify/src/`, for example `agent.rs`, `domain.rs` and `graph.rs`.\n- **The book uses the Habeas preprocessor.** The text says \"MUST use the Habeas preprocessor as specified by {cite}`requirements.cli.mdbook`\". `book.toml#table[preprocessor.habeas]/pair[command]` is marked for both requirements and sets `command = \"cargo habeas mdbook\"`. The cited requirement supplies the details: the alias and the consumer-book rule. `.cargo/config.toml` holds the alias, but that belongs to `requirements.cli.mdbook`, not to this requirement's structure.\n\nI found no further structural obligation. The text names no library, algorithm, signature or type, and the cited declaration only supplies context.\n\nbehavioral: Each obligation in `requirements.layout.project` maps to a marked test in `tests/repository.rs`.\n\n- **Markdown in `md/`:** `fn[project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias]` asserts that `book.toml` sets `book.src` to `md`. It also asserts that `md/SUMMARY.md` exists.\n- **`habeas` source in `src/`:**\n  - The same test asserts that `src/lib.rs` and `src/main.rs` exist.\n  - `fn[crate_targets_are_declared_in_src]` asserts that `Cargo.toml` declares the lib path `src/lib.rs`. It also asserts that there is exactly one bin, named `habeas`, with path `src/main.rs`.\n- **`trust-but-verify` source in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/`:** `fn[workspace_contains_frontend_and_sdk_but_not_the_vendor_fork]` asserts that `crates/trust-but-verify/src/lib.rs` exists. It asserts that the workspace members are exactly `habeas` and `trust-but-verify`. It also asserts that the dependency path is `crates/trust-but-verify`.\n- **The project's own book uses the Habeas preprocessor, as `requirements.cli.mdbook` specifies:** `fn[project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias]` asserts three things:\n  - The `habeas` preprocessor command is `cargo habeas mdbook`.\n  - Its renderers are `[\"habeas\"]`.\n  - The `.cargo/config.toml` alias `habeas` is `run --release -p habeas --`.\n\nThe cited requirement's clause that consumer books keep invoking the installed CLI concerns consumer books, not this project's layout. It is context here and needs no test.\n\nThe assertions enforce the expected outcomes. All three tests carry `{test}` markers for the subject, so I found no gap.",
